gized but things  didn't end there early in his 1992  re-election campaign President Bush told  the convention of National Religious  broadcasters we are going to keep on  trying to strengthen the American family  to make American families a lot more  like the Waltons and a lot less like The  Simpsons  a subsequent episode of The Simpsons  featured the family watching a clip of  Bush's speech hey just like  we're praying for an end to the  depression - in the season three episode  stark-raving dad homer is mistakenly  sent to a psychiatric institution where  he's befriended by a hulking balding  patient named Leon who identifies  himself as Michael Jackson he certainly  had the voice of Michael Jackson because  the real King of Pop lent his voice to  the character who are you hi I'm Michael  Jackson for the Jacksons I'm Homer  Simpson from The Simpsons in the credits  however he was billed under the name  John J Smith so how did a relatively new  TV series land the biggest pop star in  the world  Jackson simply phoned up and asked a fan  of the show Jackson at first wanted to  play himself but eventually went with  the writers when they conceived the  character of Leon the Simpsons is one of  the few successful long-running TV shows  to never have generated a spin-off but  it's not for lack of trying  in 1994 Matt Groening wrote a script for  a new series that bound Krusty the Klown  getting his own talk show and moving to  Los Angeles but it wasn't going to be a  cartoon rainin wanted it to be a  live-action series with Krusty's voice  actor dan Castellaneta reprising his  role in the flesh eventually graining  accepted it had to take the form of an  animated series instead because this  whole thing was just too expensive to  pull off in real life unfortunately the  animated show never saw the light of day  either after negotiations between  graining and Fox stalled but creativity  prevailed Brannan's next project was a  little show about Earth in the year 3000  in